    88	# <span id="Quickstart">3. Quickstart</span>
    89	
    90	The tokenizer provides a configurable chat template for reasoning and tool-use scenarios:
    91	
    92	- `enable_thinking` controls whether the model generates reasoning for the current response. It is enabled by default; set it to `False` for non-thinking mode.
    93	- `preserve_thinking` controls whether reasoning from previous assistant turns is retained in a multi-turn conversation. We recommend `False` for general chat and question answering, and `True` for multi-turn tool use, office tasks, and code-agent workflows.
    94	- Passing `tools` enables the tool-use template. We recommend `tool_call_format="xml"` for the best tool-calling performance; `json` is also supported for compatibility.
    95	
    96	The model supports a context length of up to 524,288 tokens (512K).
    97	
    98	We recommend adjusting the inference settings according to the target scenario:
    99	
   100	| Scenario | Temperature | Top_p | Max New Tokens |
   101	|---|---:|---:|---:|
   102	| Agentic and tool-use tasks | 1.0 | 0.95 | 65,536 |
   103	| Reasoning and chat tasks | 0.6 | 0.95 | 262,144 |
   104	
   105	
   106	You can run the model with Transformers, SGLang, or vLLM:
   107	
   108	## Transformers
   109	
   110	```python
   111	from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer
   112	
   113	model_id = 'Nanbeige/Nanbeige4.3-33B'
   114	tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(
   115	  model_id,
   116	  use_fast=False,
   117	  trust_remote_code=True
   118	)
   119	model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(
   120	  model_id,
   121	  torch_dtype='auto',
   122	  device_map='auto',
   123	  trust_remote_code=True
   124	)
   125	
   126	messages = [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which number is bigger, 9.11 or 9.8?'}]
   127	inputs = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(
   128	  messages,
   129	  add_generation_prompt=True,
   130	  return_tensors='pt'
   131	).to(model.device)
   132	output_ids = model.generate(inputs, max_new_tokens=1024)
   133	response = tokenizer.decode(output_ids[0][inputs.shape[-1]:], skip_special_tokens=True)
   134	print(response)
   135	```
   136	
   137	## SGLang
   138	
   139	```bash
   140	MODEL_PATH=/path/to/your/Nanbeige4.3-33B
   141	python -m sglang.launch_server \
   142	  --model-path ${MODEL_PATH} \
   143	  --host 0.0.0.0 \
   144	  --port 8000 \
   145	  --tp-size 4 \
   146	  --mem-fraction-static 0.8 \
   147	  --reasoning-parser qwen3 \
   148	  --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder
   149	```
   150	
   151	## vLLM
   152	
   153	```bash
   154	MODEL_PATH=/path/to/your/Nanbeige4.3-33B
   155	vllm serve ${MODEL_PATH} \
   156	  --host 0.0.0.0 \
   157	  --port 8000 \
   158	  --tensor-parallel-size 4 \
   159	  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.8 \
   160	  --enable-auto-tool-choice \
   161	  --reasoning-parser qwen3 \
   162	  --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder
   163	```
